WEBVTT

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:11.320
Tsubaki!

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:14.990
Noel.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:35.090
This is odd.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:36.550
There ought to be more people here.

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:39.350
Even considering the whole Grim Reaper incident.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:50.110
Makoto!

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:51.610
Is that you, Noel?

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:54.490
I found Tsubaki. I'm with her right now.

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:55.070
Huh?

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.410
I'm going to try talking to her.

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.170
Rebel 7: The Wings of Justice

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:33.090
This is Tager.
Do you copy, Kokonoe?
Rebel 7: The Wings of Justice

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:33.500
Rebel 7: The Wings of Justice

00:02:33.670 --> 00:02:36.380
Yeah, I got you. What's up?

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:39.220
I've picked up a trail. It's faint, but there.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:40.720
The Azure, huh?

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.010
Yes. I found two traces, in fact.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:45.430
They both appear to lead to the upper levels.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:48.680
Damn, so we missed each other. Go after her immediately.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.480
Get her before that bastard does, at all costs.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.520
The static is getting worse. The weather, perhaps?

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:56.860
I'm heading to the upper levels.

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:58.150
Roger that.

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:11.670
Nobody here, either...

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:15.290
You know,

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:20.010
I had no idea you'd been assigned to the Zeroth Squadron.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:27.180
Noel, the reason a member of the Wings of Justice is here in Kagutsuchi is because—

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.270
I know.

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:33.440
You came because you were ordered to kill Major Kisaragi and me.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:35.020
Noel...

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:36.690
How did that happen?

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.900
If it had just been me for acting against orders, that would be one thing, but...

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:44.660
It's an imperial command. You understand what the Imperator means to me.

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:48.620
Still, it makes no sense for you to kill Major Kisaragi.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.330
Makoto also said—

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:54.170
Then please don't resist and do as I say.

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:56.210
Let's return to HQ together.

00:03:56.210 --> 00:04:00.420
If we go now, you still might be able to have your
sentence lightened with a pardon from the Imperator.

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:05.720
I'm sorry, Tsubaki. Would you
mind waiting just a little longer?

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:06.550
Why?

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:09.180
I can't really put it into words well,

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:13.190
but I have this feeling that something really big is happening in Kagutsuchi right now.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:15.480
Are you talking about
the recent earthquake?

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:16.770
Or perhaps...

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:19.360
...the Grim Reaper incident?

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:22.240
B-Both...

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:26.120
Everything seems to be linked in some way.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:27.320
In addition,

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:31.450
I feel like I'm related to it in some way too.

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:33.830
Maybe something about the past I cannot remember.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:37.040
Have you already seen Brother Jin?

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.000
No.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:42.590
I think the Major probably went after that man.

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:44.380
Ragna the Bloodedge.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:48.890
Is it true that you've made contact with the Grim Reaper, then?

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:50.850
Yeah.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:51.930
But why?!

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:55.100
He's a rebel who's set himself against the Imperator!

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:56.350
Listen to me, Tsubaki!

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:59.770
True, he does oppose the NOL,

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:02.190
but he has his reasons to do that!

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:04.360
You're being tricked.

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:06.700
You're wrong! I can tell.

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:08.700
I know he's not a bad person.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:12.200
In fact, with the way the NOL has been acting recently, I'd say it's more—

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:12.910
Noel!

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:15.910
Do you understand the gravity of your words?

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:17.830
Supporting a rebel?

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:19.790
You may as well declare yourself in opposition to the Imperator!

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:22.210
No, it's not! I just...

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:28.340
Second Lieutenant Noel Vermillion.

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:31.010
This is an order from your superior officier.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:32.970
Return to HQ at once.

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.270
If you act against orders,

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:37.640
by my authority as an executive of the court and in the name of the Imperator,

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:40.810
I will declare you a traitor,
strip you of your rank,

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:42.820
and sentence you to permanent
banishment from the NOL.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:44.320
Tsubaki...

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:53.620
Always one to crawl in the darkness,
much like an insect.

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:55.580
Rabbit.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.540
What's wrong? Getting tired of
sitting in the peanut gallery?

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:01.250
Some scenes cannot be seen from the stage.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:02.380
Huh?

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:04.710
Follow me if you wish to know more.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.050
God...

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:16.600
Noel, Tsubaki. Please don't do
anything rash, either of you.

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:26.360
Tsubaki, please!

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:29.910
Just give me some time. Just a little more!

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:31.200
Noel.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:36.200
I understand.

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:41.420
It seems I have no choice but to force you to comply.

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.380
In my right hand, I carry the sword of judgment,

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:50.220
and in my left, the scales of justice.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.640
I serve the wings who govern the heavens.

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:56.520
I am the Wings of Justice!

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:05.900
Second Lieutenant Noel Vermillion,

00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:09.450
if you resist, your punishment will be death!

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:15.200
It appears she has donned the Izayoi.

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:20.040
Right now, all eyes have been shut out of Kagutsuchi.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.210
Now, it's time you show them your stuff.

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:26.550
First Lieutenant Tsubaki Yayoi, please fight to your heart's content.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:29.210
All it cost is your own light.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:35.430
That's...

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:38.430
The sealed armagus Izayoi.

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:41.140
A powerful armagus that has
been passed down in my family,

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:43.150
the Yayois, for generations.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:46.770
Don't do this, Tsubaki!

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:48.820
There's no point to us fighting!

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:51.950
Then don't resist and obey me, Noel!

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:53.910
Th-That's...

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:57.530
An observer, huh?

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:00.250
As well as...

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:01.960
...the Azure man.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:03.870
Who the hell are you?

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:07.340
That puppet. It's not a Nox Nyctores?

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:12.630
Did you bring me all this way just to introduce me to some pervert?

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:17.890
Relius Clover, this is not a story that you may interfere in.

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:22.350
Interfere? I merely came to witness my creation.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:25.060
What do you intend to do with her?

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.810
It was supposed to have been a defective unit.

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:30.150
And yet, it is that one that became the Azure Successor.

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:31.530
It concerns me.

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:34.450
If possible, I'd like to retrieve and examine it.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:36.990
And how is that not "interfering"?

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:40.330
Aren't <i>you</i> the one interfering here?

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:43.000
I heard you unleashed the Tsukuyomi Unit.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:50.170
The time-shearing Susano'o and the time-shielding Tsukuyomi.

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:53.800
You are in an awfully talkative mood today.

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:57.090
Hey, Rabbit, this clearly doesn't have anything to do with me, so I'm gonna just—

00:08:57.090 --> 00:08:58.720
Don't do this, Tsubaki!

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:01.640
Noel?!

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:10.860
Don't do this.

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:12.320
Tsubaki...

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:21.240
A Nox Nyctores?!

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:22.700
Why do you have one?

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:32.460
That's right, Noel.

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:34.300
You always did...

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:36.840
...stick your nose where it didn't belong!

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:40.970
Noel!

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:54.110
What's wrong, Noel?

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:55.940
Aren't you able to pull the trigger?

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:00.870
B-Bolverk...

00:10:01.830 --> 00:10:07.830
...doesn't exist to shoot...

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:09.670
...my friends!

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:13.500
Tsubaki! Let's stop this already!

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:18.470
Hey, what the flying fuck is going on here?

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:21.430
I merely came to observe my creation.

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:22.600
Your what?

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:25.270
That thing there is something I made.

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:29.140
Dimensional Boundary Interface Prime Field No. 12.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.150
It is nothing more and nothing less.

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:34.610
A Prime Field?

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:35.780
Noel?

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:44.830
She keeps on going on about friends this and friends that.

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:47.080
What a load of nonsense.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:49.080
Absolute bullshit.

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:50.710
Captain Hazama?!

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:51.880
Her words are drivel.

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:53.960
You can't let her lead you astray like that.

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:58.420
It's using those meaningless words that she steals everything away from you.

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:01.260
You graduated from the Military Academy at the top of your class

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:04.180
and come from one of the prestigious Duodecim,

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:07.390
so how come you put up with this insignificant Praetorian Guard?

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:12.730
Especially since you're part of the disposal unit, shunned even by your own!

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:16.020
I have pride in the work I do.

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:17.980
I live in service of the Imperator.

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:20.530
I have never felt discontent, not once!

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:23.200
Lying's a sin, First Lieutenant!

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:26.330
Deep inside, you feel hatred, don't you?

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:27.660
Hatred?

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:31.210
For Noel Vermillion, who stands before you.

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:32.540
N-No!

00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:34.330
Noel's my...

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:38.760
Tsubaki?

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:41.590
Utterly mediocre grades.

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:45.220
An absentminded personality completely at odds with a Praetorian Guard's duty.

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:51.100
This is the woman to whom you lost the enviable post of being Jin Kisaragi's ministral secretary!

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:53.060
I mean, c'mon! How can you not hate her?

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:55.440
Noel is my good friend.

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:57.270
I am following the Imperator's command—

00:11:57.270 --> 00:11:58.780
You saw it, did you not?!

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:00.940
When you put on the Izayoi?!

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:04.570
That was a distortion in the world.

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:08.740
In truth, <i>you</i> should have been the one standing by Jin Kisaragi's side!

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:11.250
Noel Vermillion.

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:15.380
She is a being that should not exist in this world.

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:17.590
She shouldn't exist?

00:12:17.590 --> 00:12:19.340
One who shouldn't be here.

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:21.550
No, one who <i>mustn't</i> be here.

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:25.470
She's the one who will take everything from you in this world.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:27.260
Noel!

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:30.060
I know, right?

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:31.730
That just ain't correct.

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:33.940
Better go right those wrongs.

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:35.770
And then you can die!

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:37.480
A tragic death!

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:41.570
You're nothing but a trigger to activate the dolly!

00:12:45.610 --> 00:12:48.490
The preparations for the Cauldron are now complete.

00:12:48.490 --> 00:12:51.080
I suppose it's about time we made our own move.

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:53.830
Off we go, Phantom.

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:08.050
Aurora Impact!

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:21.150
Type V!

00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:32.330
Tsubaki!

00:13:35.750 --> 00:13:37.870
A-As I thought...

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:39.960
I'm no match for you...

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:42.420
I'm sorry.

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:45.920
Why? Why do you apologize?!

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:47.930
You, who took my place...

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:50.510
Who took everything from me!

00:13:51.300 --> 00:13:52.720
Tsubaki...

00:13:52.890 --> 00:13:53.850
And even then...

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:56.430
Even then, I...

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:59.060
Charging ars magus!

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:02.320
Restraint System, disengage!

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:05.820
Stop this already!

00:14:06.190 --> 00:14:08.450
With all the power I can muster!

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:11.070
Tsubaki!

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:16.200
Mr. Ragna!

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:18.080
Ragna?!

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:19.920
The Grim Reaper, Ragna the Bloodedge?!

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:23.550
What are you doing here?

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:25.800
You two are starting to piss me off!

00:14:25.800 --> 00:14:28.010
You wanna fight or not?

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:31.970
Watching you just makes me mad.

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:33.510
Grim Reaper...

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:36.310
If only you didn't exist...

00:14:36.520 --> 00:14:37.770
Then Brother Jin wouldn't have...

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:39.640
"Brother Jin"?

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:41.610
If only you didn't exist!

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:48.570
What the hell am I doing here for?

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:52.200
Well, if you wanna keep at it, count me in for the fight.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.830
Wh-Why would you do that?!

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:56.330
Mr. Ragna, this has nothing to do with—

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:59.660
Openly expressing emotions as though you were a living thing.

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:09.630
Colonel Relius?

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:10.680
Bastard!

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:19.850
You may have succeeded the Azure, but in the end, you're still a defective unit.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.320
That fucker creeps me out!

00:15:58.390 --> 00:15:59.350
Hey.

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:00.930
You going after her? And then what?

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:03.690
She saved you a lot of trouble by leaving.

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:05.690
B-But...

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:07.480
She's my...

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:10.150
She's my friend!

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:12.860
So I have to go! I have to...

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:13.990
Jesus...

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:15.820
Go on.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:19.040
If that is what your heart dictates.

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:21.750
Ms. Rachel...

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:25.710
I don't care what you do.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:28.670
Please excuse me!

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:35.470
Hey.

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:37.850
What's up with that, Rabbit?!

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:41.060
Why'd you show me this? Was that your goal?

00:16:41.390 --> 00:16:43.390
What she really is.

00:16:43.390 --> 00:16:45.940
It's beginning to dawn on you, isn't it?

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:50.230
The color of her eyes are different.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:54.950
That's true. She's still in the pre-smelting state.

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:58.910
Right now, she's no different than an ordinary human.

00:16:59.080 --> 00:17:03.200
Now that you know, what will you do with her?

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:09.210
Reflect upon it, Ragna.

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:19.760
Shit!

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:25.690
Oh? Looks like the Izayoi's barrier is down.

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:27.440
Let's take a look!

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:32.480
What?! They're both alive?!

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:36.780
This was going to be the perfect bloodbath!

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:40.410
She's always getting crushed like a bug,

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:44.000
so I give her a little extra, but she still fails?!

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:46.370
I swear...

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:50.380
And Major Kisaragi's death was voided by a retake too.

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:52.840
What an utterly useless girl.

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:57.050
Can't count on anyone but yourself in the end, can ya?

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:03.470
Tsubaki!

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:07.520
Um...

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:09.770
Um, you know, I...

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:13.730
Tsubaki?

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:17.280
Wait, your eyes!

00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:19.410
Wh-Why?

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:21.870
That is how the Izayoi functions.

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:25.410
It's an armagus that was created to steal light in every way possible.

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:28.410
Why would you use it, then?

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:31.670
I can't win against people like Brother Jin or you.

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:34.420
I had no choice but to rely on the Izayoi.

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:35.880
But that's—

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:37.010
It's so...

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:41.090
Hey, Noel, did you know?

00:18:41.590 --> 00:18:44.220
I've always been envious of you.

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:45.180
Huh?

00:18:45.180 --> 00:18:49.480
Noel, you're much more than you take yourself for.

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:53.310
No matter how hard I worked, I could never win against you.

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:54.900
That's not true!

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:57.190
I always looked up to you.

00:18:57.190 --> 00:19:00.160
Always thinking how great it would be if I could be like you.

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:07.250
Because... Because you've always been so kind and strong and dependable.

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:11.210
Both Makoto and I really love you for that!

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:12.790
Thank you, Noel.

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:16.840
But you know, I'm not the admirable person you think I am.

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:20.380
When you ended up working alongside Brother Jin,

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:21.970
I thought of you and...

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:25.010
...wished you'd disappear, once and for all.

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:27.850
Well?

00:19:28.430 --> 00:19:30.140
You must be disappointed in me, right?

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:32.560
No, not at all.

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:35.320
I don't care. I still...

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:37.480
I still really love you, Tsubaki!

00:19:39.490 --> 00:19:41.570
Even though I tried to kill you?

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:44.990
You had no choice! You were ordered to!

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:48.620
Today...

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:52.870
Just for today, let's say that we never met.

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:56.960
But know that this is a one-time thing.

00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:07.930
Hey, Tager.

00:20:08.390 --> 00:20:09.600
Is that you, Kokonoe?

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:11.730
The comm signal is extremely unstable.

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:14.060
Is it because of the bombardment the other day?

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:15.310
No, that's not it.

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:18.520
It's something way more powerful...

00:20:18.520 --> 00:20:19.940
Kokonoe?

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:22.780
Never mind. More importantly, how's the hunt for the Azure going?

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:26.280
I've confirmed the traces.

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:30.120
As we thought, it's on the upper levels. You keep on following those tracks.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:33.500
If things go well, you might be able to rendezvous with one of our undercover agents.

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:35.080
Roger that.

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:40.920
If this comm interference is due to the sealed armagus...

00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:44.510
I swear, shit just keeps happening.

00:20:58.110 --> 00:20:59.070
Noel!

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:05.320
Thank goodness, you're all right.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:07.660
Where's Tsubaki?

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:13.580
Makoto!

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:24.010
The interminable rehearsal has come to an end

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:27.470
and I suppose we can say the story has finally reached an intermission.

00:23:01.440 --> 00:23:04.320
So, that is the sealed
armagus Izayoi?

00:23:04.320 --> 00:23:06.150
It is quite a fine soul.

00:23:06.150 --> 00:23:09.030
Episode 8,
"The Mechanical Soul".

00:23:09.030 --> 00:23:11.110
Izayoi spoke?!
